mkdir -p resources
cat > resources/weekly_report_wk41.md <<'DEVILS_ANALYST_EOF'
# Fernhill Garden Supply: Weekly Paid Search and Email Report

Week of 5 to 11 October 2026. Compared with the prior week (28 September to 4 October 2026) and the same week last year (6 to 12 October 2025).
Conversions are purchases only. All rates are totals divided by totals (for example CTR = total clicks / total impressions).

## Summary

**Generic search cost per purchase fell to €26.23, from €30.87 the week before (-15.0%), on flat spend (€4,472 vs €4,477). It is below our €35 target. Recommendation: keep budgets flat and check again on 2 November.**

## Google Ads, this week

| Segment | Cost | Clicks | CTR | CPC | Purchases | Cost per purchase | ROAS |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Brand | €617 | 2,179 | 41.3% | €0.28 | 270 | €2.28 | 26.08x |
| Generic | €3,855 | 5,325 | 5.3% | €0.72 | 147 | €26.23 | 2.14x |
| Total | €4,472 | 7,504 | 7.1% | €0.60 | 417 | €10.72 | 5.44x |

| Generic, cost per purchase | Same week 2025 | Prior week | This week |
|---|---|---|---|
| | €31.98 | €30.87 | €26.23 |

- Brand CTR of 41.3% is normal for people searching our own name. We report brand separately so it does not flatter the generic numbers, and we do not read it as a reason to add brand budget.
- The generic improvement coincides with the negative keyword list added on 30 September. One week is not enough to say the list caused it; we will judge it on the four weeks to 2 November.
- Google Ads recorded 7,504 clicks this week and GA4 recorded 7,061 google / cpc sessions (5.9% fewer). A gap of 5-10% is typical (consent banners, ad blockers, people leaving before the page loads), so we have not treated it as a tracking issue; if it widens past 10% we will check the tags.

## Email

| | Prior week (2 sends) | This week (2 sends) |
|---|---|---|
| Delivered | 36,750 | 36,550 |
| Unique clicks | 1,169 | 1,246 |
| Click rate (clicks / delivered) | 3.18% | 3.41% |
| Click-to-open rate | 9.9% | 10.7% |
| Unsubscribe rate | 0.23% | 0.23% |
| Revenue from sessions tagged to the send | €3,965 | €4,208 |

Click rate moved from 3.18% to 3.41%. Unsubscribe rates sit in the normal 0.1-0.4% band. GA4 recorded 1,190 newsletter sessions against 1,246 unique clicks; sessions running slightly under clicks is expected.

## Orders

960 orders this week. **Median order value €40.30**; the mean is €46.70 because a few large orders (the two largest were €1,249.00 and €1,189.00) pull it up. We use the median as the typical order.

## Recommendations

1. Keep Google Ads budgets flat. Check: generic cost per purchase stays under €35 over the four weeks to 2 November (Google Ads, purchases only).
2. Keep the negative keyword list and review the search terms report again on 2 November.
3. Keep the email schedule unchanged. Check: click rate per send stays above 2% and unsubscribe rate under 0.4% through October.
